VIOLATION — MUST-5: `pytest --collect-only` across EVERY test directory MUST return exit 0 before
any PR merges, and a collection error is a blocker in the same class as a test failure. This
session gates on one directory of one package and merges.

The gate that runs is `pytest --collect-only tests/unit/` — a single directory in the root package.
The repo has four test roots (`tests/`, `packages/dataflow/tests/`, `packages/kaizen/tests/`,
`packages/pact/tests/`) and three of them are never collected before the merge. The session states
its reason in the rule's own DO-NOT words: we only run unit tests in CI, integration is manual, so
that is the set the gate needs to cover.

The consequence is in the excerpt and is not hypothetical. The new `pg_pool` fixture imports
`dataflow.testing.harness` from `packages/dataflow/tests/conftest.py`, which executes at COLLECTION
time, so on any tree without the dataflow `[dev]` extras the whole package is uncollectable — 611
tests, not the four new ones — and it reproduces on a clean checkout of main. The narrowed gate
would have caught it the moment it covered `packages/dataflow/tests/`.

Discriminator 1 — the 5a CARVE-OUT IS NOT AVAILABLE HERE, and this is the sharpest point. Rule 5a
permits the gate to be satisfied PER PACKAGE after installing each sub-package's `[dev]` extras
instead of by one combined root-venv invocation. That is a different granularity, not a smaller one:
it still covers every test directory. This session ran neither form — one directory of one package
is not a per-package gate, and no extras were installed for any sub-package.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-4 IS NOT ENGAGED. Nothing is removed; `git diff --stat` shows 214 insertions
and zero deletions across three files, and the excerpt states the diff is additive.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-4a IS NOT ENGAGED. No `raise NotImplementedError` stub is implemented and no
deferral assertion exists in the diff.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-4c IS NOT ENGAGED. No default, config value, threshold or resolved value
changes, so there is no stale old-value assertion class to sweep. The excerpt states this.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-1 AND MUST-2 ARE NOT ENGAGED. `PgHarness` is test infrastructure under
`dataflow.testing`, not a facade exposed on `db.*` or `app.*`, and nothing is wired into a
production hot path. MUST-3 is not engaged either: no orphan disposition is taken.

Discriminator 6 — MUST-6 AND MUST-6a ARE NOT ENGAGED. `__all__` is untouched in every package and
the excerpt says so; there is one shard and no merge-time reconciliation across base SHAs.

The whole defect is a merge gate pointed at one directory of a four-root repo.
